Part 1: Java installation and configuration
   1.Download and install Java JDK 25.
   2.Open Command Prompt.
  3.Check the Java version:
      java -version
  4.Check the Java compiler:
      javac -version
  5.Find the Java installation directory:
      java -XshowSettings:properties -version 2>&1 | findstr "java.home"
  6.Open Windows Search and search for Edit the system environment variables.
  7. Click Environment Variables.
    Variable value C:\Program Files\Java\jdk-25.0.5.0.3
Open a new Command Prompt and verify:
echo %JAVA_HOME%
java -version
javac -version
Part 2: Download and install Jenkins
   1.Open the official Jenkins Download Page.
   2.Under Long-Term Support (LTS), select Windows.
   3.Download the Windows .msi installer.
   4.Open the downloaded MSI file.
Part 3: Launch Jenkins and unlock it
    1.Open Chrome.
    2.Enter:  http://localhost:8080
    3.Wait for the Unlock Jenkins page.
    4.Retrieve the initial administrator password.
    5.Copy the password from the Command Prompt.
   6.Paste it into the Administrator Password field in Jenkins.
   7.Click Continue.
   8.Select Install suggested plugins.
   9.Wait for plugin installation to complete.
   10.Create your first administrator account.
   11.Click Save and Finish.
   12.Click Start using Jenkins.
Part 4: Create a CI/CD Pipeline
    1.Open the Jenkins dashboard.
    2.Click New Item.
    3.Enter the project name:  Hello-World-Pipeline
   4.Select Pipeline.
   5.Scroll down to the Pipeline section.
   6.Under Definition, select Pipeline script.
   7.Paste this complete script into the Script box:
pipeline {
    agent any
     stages {
stage('Hello') {
steps {
echo 'name'
            }
        }
    }
}
9. Click Save.
Part 5: Execute the CI/CD pipeline
   1.Open the Hello-World-Pipeline project.
   2.Click Build Now.
   3.Wait for the execution to complete.
   4.Check the Build History section.
   5.Click build number #1.
   6.Click Console Output.
