*Install VirtualBox
Verify installation:
  Open CMD and type:
    VBoxManage --version  (You should see the installed VirtualBox version.)
*Install Minikube
 Open Command Prompt.
   1.Check Winget:
       winget --version
  2.Install Minikube:
       winget install -e --id Kubernetes.minikube
  3.If it asks for permission, type Y and press Enter.
  4.Wait until installation finishes.
  5.Close CMD and open it again.
  6.Check Minikube installation:
      minikube version
*Install kubectl
   Open Command Prompt.
   1.Check Winget (if already checked, skip this).
       winget --version
   2.Install kubectl:
       winget install -e --id Kubernetes.kubectl
  3.If it asks for permission, type Y and press Enter.
  4.Wait for installation to complete.
  5.Close CMD and open it again.
  6.Verify installation:
      kubectl version --client
*Open Command Prompt (again)
   Check Minikube installation
     minikube version
   1.Start Minikube cluster using VirtualBox
       minikube start --driver=virtualbox
  2.Check the status of the cluster
       minikube status
  3.Check Kubernetes nodes
       kubectl get nodes
  4.Create and deploy an application
       kubectl create deployment nginx --image=nginx
  5.Check the running pods
       kubectl get pods
  6.Check the deployment
      kubectl get deployments
Open CMD and enter:
   kubectl expose deployment nginx --type=NodePort --port=80
Check the available services
   kubectl get services
Access the application
   minikube service nginx
This command will open the Nginx application in your default web browser.
Minikube stop
