*Download docket desktop and gitbash
   Check Docker:  docker --version
   Check Git: git --version
 Clone the GitHub project
    Open CMD.
      git clone https://github.com/docker/getting-started-todo-app
    Press Enter.
 Navigate into the project folder
      Enter: cd getting-started-todo-app
      To check the files, enter: dir
Start the development environment
    docker compose watch
Press Enter and wait.
    Open your browser:
    Open the Docker To-Do application
      You should see a To-Do application where you can add and delete tasks.
    Develop with containers 
    Check containers in Docker Desktop
      1.Open Docker Desktop.
      2.Click Containers in the left sidebar.
      3.Find the getting-started-todo-app application group.
      4.Expand it to view the running containers.
Build a Docker image
    docker build -t welcome .
Before running it, open a second CMD window and navigate into the project directory:
   cd getting-started-todo-app
Check whether a Dockerfile exists:
   dir Dockerfile
If it exists, execute:
   docker build -t welcome .
To check the images:
   docker images
Step 7: Stop the application
Go back to the first CMD window where docker compose watch is running.
Press:
Ctrl + C
Then enter:
docker compose down
This stops and removes the application's containers and network.
